From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:53:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 171/174] feat(gastown): ship the polecat preflight and
 self-review gates as one pack executable (gcp-v9mvh)

The preflight-tests section-1 fence (136 lines) and the self-review
section-2 fence (91 lines) were shell the model retyped on every polecat
run: measured at 18.4K and 14.9K output tokens per bead, and four of four
preflight runs between 22:06Z and 01:40Z dropped a space while retyping
and reported a false raw:gate(test): FAIL (winnow-fwxxak).

Both fences now run as gastown/assets/scripts/polecat-gates.sh with a
`preflight` and a `self-review` mode and ONE copy of resolve-known-red,
gate-run and known-red-phase-skip. Each formula step carries a short stub
that finds the script the way resolve_known_red already finds known-red
(gc formula list --json -> source -> dirname twice; formula step text gets
no Go-template fields, and GC_PACK_DIR is not exported to agent shells) and
passes the rig's commands as PG_* env, so no {{var}} survives in the script.
The self-review stub also exports BASE_REF, so a set-but-unexported
BASE_REF still reaches the script and affected_tests_command.

Behaviour is identical on every path but one: when the formula cannot be
resolved the step now stops (STOP + drain-ack + exit 1) where the old
fence warned that known-red was missing and ran the gates anyway. The stub
and the script ship together, so only a city layer overriding
mol-polecat-work or a broken gc can reach it. preflight-tests joins
self-review in DEFERRED_STEPS for that early exit.

Validation: a throwaway identity harness (not committed) renders the old
fence and the new stub from each tree and diffs stdout, stderr, exit code,
the gc/known-red call log and the gate log over 26 paths: 26 same, 0 differ,
and a one-word mutation of the script turns two of them into DIFF.
test_known_red_wiring.sh now reads the polecat blocks from the script by
sentinel; test_polecat_gates.sh covers usage, required-var handling, the
empty affected-tests fallback and both stubs' unresolved-script stop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
